// proves a `@derive`d quote admitting TWO top-level declarations
// gives the first one its own expression range: a method on the
// second's answer (a Cell built by the first, free-standing fn) once
// read as "a method on a nameless receiver survived typing" — the
// first declaration's body reading back empty because the second's
// range swallowed it.
use @std.meta.{derive}
use @test.sibling_floor.{MakesCell}

@derive(MakesCell)
type Foo = { x: int }

"${Foo.read_cell()}"
